# The chip answers to the configuration it was formatted against, which is not
# always the one this model ships - a handset whose secure element was
# provisioned elsewhere needs that set instead. init.sony.rc binds by model;
# this binds whatever XperiaParts was told to use on top of it.
#
# Lives on system_ext because the property has to be writable by the settings
# app: /vendor and /odm scripts expand ${} through vendor_init, which cannot
# read a system property, and a vendor property cannot be set from an app at
# all. init parses this one itself, so it can read either.
#
# The name is shared with every other device that ships this, which is why it
# carries no vendor segment: the same setprop works on joan_jp, where a model
# is spelled as an LG SKU instead.
on property:persist.felica.model=*
    mount none /vendor/etc/felica_${persist.felica.model} /vendor/etc/felica bind
